  "text": "Test 3\nQuestions 9-13\nLook at the following statements (Questions 9-13) and the list ofpeople below.\nMatch each statement with the correct person, A, B, C or D.\nWrite the correct letter, A, B, C or D, in boxes 9-13 on your answer sheet.\nNB\nYou may use any letter more than once.\n9\nThe environmental advantage of cement alternatives may not be as great as\ninitially assumed.\n10\nIt would be hard to create a construction alternative to concrete that offers so many\ncomparable benefits.\n11.\nWorries about the environment have led to increased interest in wood as a\nconstruction material.\n12\nExpense has beena factor in the negative response to the development of\nnew cements.\n13\nThe environmental damage caused by concrete is due to it being produced in\nlarge quantities.\nList of People\nA\nChris Cheeseman\nB\nMarkus Mannstr6m\nC_\nAnna Surgenor\nD_\nFelix Preston and Johanna Lehne\n64\n>|@ p. 124\n",
